{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>gods whom they did not know</b> — they did not know divine power in them, and He did not allot to them nor assign them as their portion. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Deuteronomy 29:25) translated it: וְלֹא אוֹטִיב לְהוֹן — 'he did no good for them.' And according to the language of <b>חָלַק</b>, that deity which they chose for themselves did not allot them any inheritance or portion — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 29:25). But the correct interpretation is: <b>gods whom they did not know</b> as gods — that is, they did not know them to possess any divine power arising from themselves, and יהוה the Elohim of their fathers did not apportion them to them, for He did not appoint them as officers over Israel as He appointed them over the nations. And I have already explained this (Leviticus 18:25)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:42.512171589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}